# Worker input & pointer architecture

## Lanes (strict priority)

| Lane | Messages | Handler |
|------|----------|---------|
| Pointer | `inject-pointer-click`, `pointer-crdt-deliver` | Priority bootstrap → `sceneWorker` deliver queue |
| Keyboard | `scene-input-snapshot`, `pump-scene-engine-tick` | Normal worker message path |
| Cooperative | `renderer-inbound-deliver`, RPC, boot | Normal path |

Main posts freely. Worker owns ordering via `sceneWorkerInputSession` (snapshots coalesce during pointer session).

## Ui CRDT egress boundary (hard rule)

Scene UI **CRDT wire** bytes (`UiTransform`, `UiBackground`, `UiText`, `UiInput`, `UiDropdown`, `PointerEvents`) must not leave the worker on cooperative `rpcCrdt` (phases 1–3 / play cold CRDT). `stripSceneUiCrdtBytes` strips them.

Structured mount snapshots (`collectWorkerUiMountSnapshot` → `postUiMountSnapshot` / pointer phase-4) are the only UI transport:

- **Pointer phase 4** — after every inject click (open/close menus).
- **Cooperative dirty** — when worker UI fingerprint changes (hydration splash + play-mode async updates: QR texture mint, remote preset lists, timers). Not CRDT wire.

Never emit Ui* CRDT mid pointer phases 1–3.

## Pointer egress buffers

During pointer defer (`shouldDeferPointerOutbound`):

- Phases 1–3 → `pointerDeferredNonUi` (Ui* stripped)
- Phase 4 → `collectWorkerUiMountSnapshot` → `pointerUiMountSnapshot`; non-Ui remainder → `pointerDeferredNonUi`

`flushPointerDeferredOutboundsAsync`:

1. Post all non-Ui chunks (no `uiEntities`)
2. Post **one** atomic Ui snapshot last with `uiMountSnapshot + uiEntities` (empty CRDT data)
3. Await all `crdt-outbound-ack` before `pointer-deliver-done`

No gap force-flush, no shrink skip, no mid-tick Ui emit.

## Pointer interactive tick (Explorer press lifecycle — all scenes)

**One universal edge pipeline** — no per-scene / per-genre branches. Browser is source of truth:

```text
pointerdown → inject phase=down → eng.update(0) → deliver-done
  (isPressed sticky; cooperative play frames keep running)
pointerup   → inject phase=up   → eng.update(0) → deliver-done
  (getClick / onPointerUp this frame)
```

`runSceneEnginePointerTick` + `executePointerEdge` (worker):

1. Apply **PrimaryPointerInfo** from inject body (live screen/ray for this edge) on RootEntity
2. Inject **one** PET edge (`down` or `up`) immediately before `engine.update(0)`
3. **Never** `exports.onUpdate` / pollEvents on the inject path (replays UI toggles / flight off)
4. If UI fingerprint dirty **or** `sceneUi`: bounded fingerprint settle (≤2 passes) + `runPointerUiPhase4Egress` (structured mount only). **World PE must also phase-4** — unit/building select mutates react-ecs HUD without `sceneUi=true`
5. Non-Ui light phase; **immediate** `pointer-deliver-done` — no multi-second CRDT-ack freeze for holds
6. Cooperative ticks **must keep running while the mouse is held** (`isPressed` needs play frames)

**PPI on edges:** many scenes gate select/move on `PrimaryPointerInfo` (UI chrome hit-test, ground ray from `worldRayDirection`). Play-frame-tick alone is not enough when edges run between play frames — main must attach `primaryPointer` on every `inject-pointer-click`.

**VC bind hydrate:** graph key is structure-only (entity/lookAt/parent). Continuous pan pose rides `vc-pose-live` — never re-hydrate every frame.

**Hard rules:**

- Do **not** open a long-lived pointer input session spanning mouse hold (that sets `pointerBlocksEngineTick` and freezes particles/VC/tweens).
- Do **not** default `sceneTicksPaused` for ordinary PE edges.
- UI CRDT: still strip on cooperative; phase-4 structured snapshot only when dirty.
- `sceneUi` flag only changes **UP target resolution** (PlayerEntity clear), not freeze policy.
- Same-tick DOWN+UP (`phase=click`) is deprecated; main always flushes split edges.

Sticky `inputSystem.isPressed` + per-frame edges match `@dcl/ecs` for **every** scene.

**Pointer hold reassert:** after phase=down, worker tracks held buttons and re-fires
`PET_DOWN` each `play-frame-tick` (same as keyboard). Without this, a quick click never
leaves a play frame with `isPressed` true and hold/click-move systems no-op. Clear on phase=up.

Components are independent — no cross-component input gating.

- **MainCamera** (`reconcileMainCameraCrdtEgress`, `installVirtualCameraBindGuard`): lens projection / VIEW SHOT bind only. Stale `{}` clears must not override an active bind. RETURN TO PLAYER clears run in pointer non-Ui phase (pointer input session open). **No input role.**
- **InputModifier** (`player-frame` hot path + optional `reconcileInputModifierCrdtEgress`): **scene-authoritative**. Do not latch/re-apply freeze on the worker — camera-operator re-freezes every frame while MOVE CAMERA is active; a shim latch blocked STOP permanently. Main `readLocomotionFromComponents` → `PlayerSystem` blocks avatar locomotion/emotes. **No MainCamera coupling.**
- **SceneInputRelay**: keyboard level-state to worker `inputSystem` — gated only by UI typing / overlay (`isRelayBlocked`), not by MainCamera or VC bind. Flight keys (`scene-input-snapshot` with WASD) apply immediately even during a pointer input session. While flight keys are held, `pump-scene-engine-tick` runs worker `engine.update` only (VirtualCameraRig is `engine.addSystem`; do **not** run full `exports.onUpdate` / pollEvents mid-flight — it replays UI clicks and toggles flight off).

Pointer deferred non-Ui chunks are LWW-coalesced, then each reconcile runs as its own pass at `flushPointerDeferredOutboundsAsync`. Worker `rendererInboundApply` strips worker-authoritative inbound (`InputModifier`, `MainCamera`) so main does not echo during pointer session.

## Pointer timestamps

All worker `PointerEventsResult` rows use `workerPointerEventTimestamp.ts`. UI clicks: `inject-pointer-click` only.

## Pointer delivery & tick resume

- `flushPointerDeferredOutboundsAsync` awaits `crdt-outbound-ack` (after main apply) before `pointer-deliver-done`.
- Main sets `pointerHoldTicksUntilMount` on deliver; resumes via `pause-scene-ticks:false` only when `isMountSetReady`.
- `pause-scene-ticks:false` ends pointer input session (keyboard coalesce) + `flushDeferredRendererInbound({ applyOnly: true })`.
- Bulk mount: `clearLwwSlotsForEntities` on main before apply when `mountChanged` or pointer-open batch.

## Do not

- Shrink heuristics (`suppressShrink`, `pointer ui shrink skipped`) — hard strip instead
- Transport gap force-flush or `pointer-input-session-end` maze
- `deferUiEmit`, `pendingSceneInputSnapshot`, or cooperative tick resume before mount commit
- Mid-tick Ui CRDT emit during pointer delivery
- Defensive belt-and-suspenders paths — fix phase boundaries instead